      "text": "The year 1856 is the pivot point. William Henry Perkin, an 18-year-old chemistry student attempting to synthesize quinine, produced a purple sludge from coal tar aniline — mauveine. Within 40 years, the entire pre-industrial natural dye industry collapsed."
    },
